    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n90297" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρόσφαγμα</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ατος</span>,
			τό, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>victim sacrificed for</i> others, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τύμβῳ πρόσφαγμα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Hec.</u>
					41
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θεᾷ π</span>. <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>IT</u>
				243
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Comp.Thes.Rom.</u>
				1
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				2
			</span></i>): pl., of a single victim, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Hec.</u>
				265
			</span></i>; of the victim's blood, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Alc.</u>
				845
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>sacrifice, slaughter</i>, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Ag.</u>
				1278
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Tr.</u>
				628
			</span></i> (pl.).</div>
